{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/003-implementor.json | sed -n '1,500p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t{\"command\":\"story-implement\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"8aa56afe-03ec-4da6-a2e8-2d6f10d67bd3\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"role\":\"story_implementor\",\"sessionId\":\"11cfbce6-8c6f-47e4-8ae9-6d1d829e88b4\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"sessionId\":\"11cfbce6-8c6f-47e4-8ae9-6d1d829e88b4\",\"storyId\":\"05-message-edit-cascade\"},\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"05-message-edit-cascade\",\"title\":\"Story 5: Message Edit and Cascade\"},\"planSummary\":\"Implemented Story 5 (message edit and cascade): a new shared cascade module (src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts) derives the clear-set structurally from the message → turn → chunk walk over existing derived_form rows, supersede-deletes still-queued old-version items (reported on the result), and enqueues replacements at each group's max source version + 1 inside the mutation's transaction. messages.edit validates through the deleted-filtered read (turn_open / message_not_found refusals), applies content + blocks + token re-stamp via new store.ts helpers (readMutableMessage / applyMessageEdit mirroring projectEvent's counted fields), runs the cascade, and returns the MutationResult — one synchronous commit, with enqueue pokes riding onCommit so background mode rebuilds with no further call. The source-version check (existing single write path in work-queue complete()) is provoked by TC-5.4's delayed-double recipe: a real claimed pre-edit item held across the edit completes after the post-edit replacement is queued and discards as stale_discarded. CLI: new src/cli/messages-mutate.ts and `lhc messages edit --message/--message-id --content` wiring with parity proven through the spawned binary.\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts\",\"reason\":\"NEW: walk-and-clear cascade module (DD-8) — structural chain enumeration, supersede-delete of queued old-version items, replacement enqueues at next source version\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts\",\"reason\":\"edit's validation read (readMutableMessage, deleted-filtered, joined turn status) and record apply (applyMessageEdit: block content update + token re-stamp via the one estimator)\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"messages.edit operation (one runInTransaction: validate → apply → cascade) and the MutationResult interface\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/cli/messages-mutate.ts\",\"reason\":\"NEW per §Placement: runMessagesEdit mirroring the SDK operation one-for-one\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"`lhc messages edit` command wiring, --message/--message-id and --content flags, HELP line\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"reason\":\"export MutationResult type on the public surface\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/vitest.config.ts\",\"reason\":\"exclude the new cli-process-mutations suite outside LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1, matching the other process suites\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/mutations.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"NEW: TC-5.1 through TC-5.5 plus the induced-failure atomicity leg and a background-mode edit-and-walk-away production-path test\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/cli-process-mutations.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"NEW: TC-5.6 SDK/CLI twin parity (result JSON, cascade rows, read-back) plus CLI refusal parity\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\",\"reason\":\"recorded the two new test files' hashes (green may add files; the record step locks them)\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[\"test/mutations.test.ts — TC-5.1: synchronous content/blocks/estimate update, cleared + queued named on the result, rebuild derives from edited content\",\"test/mutations.test.ts — TC-5.1 atomicity (architecture risk): induced cascade failure (planted claimed row at the replacement id) rolls back the content change too; full snapshot byte-stable\",\"test/mutations.test.ts — TC-5.2 (architecture risk): two-chunk thread, cleared set exactly 5 forms (message + turn's 2 + chunk 1's 2); every form outside the chain deep-equal pre-edit including source version\",\"test/mutations.test.ts — TC-5.3: post-return all dependents pending, replacement ids carry the new source version; second edit supersedes the still-queued first wave, rows deleted, ids reported\",\"test/mutations.test.ts — TC-5.4 (epic's named architecture-risk test): delayed double holds a claimed pre-edit smoothing across the edit; old and replacement items coexist (version-scoped ids); drain report shows stale_discarded then done; exactly one ready row from post-edit content\",\"test/mutations.test.ts — TC-5.5: turn_open and message_not_found refusals plus deleted-target-reads-as-message_not_found; snapshot (messages + forms + queue) identical after each\",\"test/mutations.test.ts — background-mode edit-and-walk-away: cascade pokes ride the commit; rebuilds run with no further call (production path proof)\",\"test/cli-process-mutations.test.ts — TC-5.6: same edit via SDK and spawned CLI on twin fixtures: identical result JSON, identical queue rows (minus wall-clock queuedAt), identical message and form read-back\",\"test/cli-process-mutations.test.ts — TC-5.6 refusal parity: CLI exits 1 with the same stable message_not_found code; record unchanged\"],\"modified\":[],\"removed\":[],\"totalAfterStory\":217,\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\":9},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm vitest run test/mutations.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm vitest run test/cli-process-mutations.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"selfReview\":{\"passesRun\":0,\"findingsFixed\":[\"Atomicity fault injection initially targeted a queued conflicting row, which the cascade's supersede step would have deleted before the enqueue; switched to a claimed row so the replacement insert genuinely collides mid-cascade and forces the rollback path\",\"Cascade source-version bump computed per rebuild group as max(existing versions) + 1 rather than per-form +1, so the two turn forms (one shared turn_derivation item) can never enqueue at diverged versions\"],\"findingsSurfaced\":[\"TC-5.4 timing: the edit must land inside the delayed double's 400ms provider window after the poll observes the handler start; edit completes in single-digit milliseconds so the margin is wide, but an extremely loaded CI machine could in principle let the v1 completion land first and fail the mid-flight coexistence assertion\",\"messages.listMessages and turns reads do not yet filter deleted_at (Story 6 scope); TC-5.5's deleted-target leg stamps deleted_at below the SDK and only asserts the edit refusal reads through the filtered validation view\"]},\"openQuestions\":[],\"specDeviations\":[\"TC-5.6's CLI parity legs live in a new test/cli-process-mutations.test.ts instead of test/cli-process-work.test.ts named by the story's test mapping: that file is hash-locked by the Story 1 red manifest (green may add files, not edit) — same precedent Story 4 set with cli-process-report-repair.test.ts\",\"TC-5.4 holds the claimed pre-edit item via an unawaited manual-mode work.drain promise rather than background mode + drainSettled, so the drain report's stale_discarded disposition is directly assertable (the test plan's storage-contract note requires that assertion); the claimed-item-held-across-the-edit overlap is identical, and background mode is separately proven by the edit-and-walk-away test\",\"CLI accepts both --message (the story's and tech design's spelling) and --message-id (the house convention used by report/requeue); both parse into the same input\",\"For tool_call blocks the edit's content string lands verbatim as the new arguments value (estimate re-stamped from its serialization, mirroring projection); the design's edit signature is content: string for all kinds and only text-kind edits are TC-covered — noted for the Story 6/verifier record\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Proceed to story verification; then Story 6 (delete) can reuse cascadeFromMessage's walk with the dropped-forms close path\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/003-implementor.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T05:57:21.029Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T06:14:31.156Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
